.TH sane\-finet 5 "6 Sep 2026" "@PACKAGEVERSION@" "SANE Scanner Access Now Easy"
.IX sane\-finet
.SH NAME
sane\-finet \- SANE backend for the network interface of Ricoh fi\-8000 series scanners
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sane\-finet
library implements a SANE (Scanner Access Now Easy) backend which drives
Ricoh (formerly Fujitsu/PFU) fi\-8000 series document scanners, such as
the fi\-8950, through their Ethernet interface. It uses the HTTP/JSON
protocol which the vendor's PaperStream IP Net driver speaks; no vendor
software is needed.
.PP
The scanner always delivers colour JPEG images at the requested
resolution, so greyscale and lineart output are produced by the backend.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The backend finds scanners on the local network automatically, by
broadcasting a probe, so usually no configuration is needed. A scanner
on another subnet, or one that should be used without the broadcast, is
listed in
.I @CONFIGDIR@/finet.conf
by address:
.PP
.RS
device 192.168.1.50
.br
device scanner.example.com:80
.RE
.PP
A scanner can also be opened directly with a device name of the form
.IR finet:address .
The line
.B option no-discovery
in the configuration file turns off the automatic search.
.SH OPTIONS
.B \-\-source
selects
.IR "ADF Front" ", " "ADF Back" " or " "ADF Duplex" ;
in duplex each sheet gives two images. The feeder runs continuously
from the first
.BR sane_start ()
until the hopper is empty or the scan is cancelled. The usual mode,
resolution and
scan area options follow. The scanner only produces colour JPEG, so
greyscale and lineart are made from that in the backend, lineart with
.BR \-\-threshold .
.PP
.B \-\-auto\-size
makes the backend detect each sheet's size and crop the image to it,
instead of using the scan area. The sheet is scanned against the
scanner's black backing so the page edges can be found, and the
scan-area and background-colour options are then ignored.
.PP
.B \-\-deskew
lets the scanner straighten skewed pages.
.B \-\-brightness
and
.B \-\-contrast
run from \-127 to 127 and are applied while decoding.
.PP
.B \-\-compression
hands the scanner's JPEG over as a SANE_FRAME_JPEG frame instead of
decoding it (colour only, and only when no brightness or contrast
adjustment is set), and
.B \-\-jpeg\-quality
sets the quality of the JPEG the scanner produces.
.B \-\-bg\-color
chooses the white or black backing seen beyond the edges of the paper.
.B \-\-df\-detect
stops the scan when the ultrasonic sensor finds two sheets feeding at
once, and
.B \-\-prepick
feeds the next sheet to the pick position early, for speed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @CONFIGDIR@/finet.conf
The backend configuration file.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane\-finet.a
The static library implementing this backend.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane\-finet.so
The shared library implementing this backend (present on systems that
support dynamic loading).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SANE_CONFIG_DIR
This environment variable specifies the list of directories that may
contain the configuration file.
.TP
.B SANE_DEBUG_FINET
If the library was compiled with debug support enabled, this
environment variable controls the debug level for this backend.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sane (7),
.BR sane\-fujitsu (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Simon Glass
